            <p>Tung Chung → Central: ~30 min | Central → Tung Chung: ~30 min | Allow 30 min to get from hotel to airport.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="subsection">
        <h4>Option A — Hong Kong Island & Kowloon</h4>
        <div class="card">
            <p class="note">Best for iconic city sights — skyline, harbour, Peak views and local food.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>9:00 AM</strong> — Checkout hotel, grab Octopus Card, MTR to Central (~30 min)</li>
                <li><strong>9:30 AM</strong> — 🥟 Dim sum breakfast at Tim Ho Wan or local cha chaan teng in Sheung Wan</li>
                <li><strong>10:30 AM</strong> — 🚠 <strong>Victoria Peak</strong> — take the historic Peak Tram funicular up. Stunning 180-degree views over Victoria Harbour, Kowloon and the surrounding hills. Best in the morning before heat and haze. ~1.5 hours | Book tram tickets in advance online to skip queues!</li>
                <li><strong>12:00 PM</strong> — ⛴️ <strong>Star Ferry</strong> — cross Victoria Harbour to Tsim Sha Tsui (Kowloon). One of the 50 must-visit experiences in a lifetime. Only HK$3, takes 8 minutes, incredible skyline views.</li>
                <li><strong>12:30 PM</strong> — Stroll the <strong>Tsim Sha Tsui waterfront promenade</strong> — Avenue of Stars, harbour views, iconic skyline photography</li>
                <li><strong>1:00 PM</strong> — 🍜 Lunch in Tsim Sha Tsui — dim sum or Cantonese noodles at a local spot</li>
                <li><strong>2:00 PM</strong> — MTR back to Tung Chung (~35 min)</li>
                <li><strong>2:45 PM</strong> — Collect luggage at hotel</li>
                <li><strong>3:30 PM</strong> — Head to airport for CX 812 (departs 7:10 PM)</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="tip"><strong>💡 Tips:</strong> Dress light — late June/July is hot and humid in HK. Book Peak Tram online in advance, queues can be very long without a reservation. Octopus Card covers all transport seamlessly.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

